# Line-ending policy.
#
# Why this file exists: this machine runs with core.autocrlf=true and had no
# .gitattributes, so checkouts were CRLF while the committed blobs were LF. The
# committed content was always fine, but the mixed working state caused real
# damage once: scripts/inline-hooks.js strips a leading shebang with /^#!.*\n/,
# and `.` does not match `\r`, so on a CRLF checkout the strip silently failed
# and the shebang got inlined into the middle of both generated hooks, making
# them unparseable. Declaring the policy here removes the whole class.
#
# The repository is published, so normalise to LF everywhere; the blobs already
# are LF, which means this changes checkouts but not the published content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.pptx binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary
